  "preamble": "Devoicing of the voiced alveolar affricate [dz] to [ts]. It occurs as word-final obstruent devoicing in Polish, where wódz 'leader' is [vut͡s], and as an unconditioned historical change in Mandarin and Changsha Xiang, where Middle Chinese voiced dz- became unaspirated ts- in syllables of the oblique tones, as in 坐 MC dzwaX > Mandarin zuò [t͡suo], Changsha [t͡so].",
